        "original_id": "c058ad27-74fe-567c-a4c5-30360a737758",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Jalalabad, Kotli Loharan East, Pakistan, Afghanistan, Punjab\n- People: Pashtun diaspora\n- Languages: Pashto\n- Topics: Pashtun communities\n\nFacts:\n- In the 7th century, Hsüan-tsang documented Jalalabad as formerly being called Ādīnapūr.\n- Jalalabad is a city in eastern Afghanistan.\n- Kotli Loharan East is a town in the Punjab province of Pakistan.\n- Pakistan is home to the largest Pashtun community.\n- Pashto is the main language among the Pashtun diaspora around the world.",
